{
  "page": 11,
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "SCALABLE KOOPMAN REACHABILITY WITH CONFORMAL COVERAGE GUARANTEES",
      "bbox": [
        126.10299682617188,
        41.200374603271484,
        483.1772155761719,
        50.106937408447266
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "3D Quadcopter",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        94.29376220703125,
        162.31643676757812,
        104.10104370117188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We evaluate an analytical 12-state quadcopter (14) (Sabatino, 2015) navigating",
      "bbox": [
        173.2255401611328,
        94.42467498779297,
        522.0001831054688,
        104.17741394042969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "around a 1 m radius obstacle for T = 200. Here, ϕ and ψ have 3 hidden layers with 128 neurons",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        107.188232421875,
        521.9894409179688,
        118.09732818603516
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "each, and z ∈R24. The computed CKRS (Fig. 4) verifies safety and goal reaching; metrics are in Ta-",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        118.98250579833984,
        521.9976806640625,
        139.3917999267578
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ble 1. To show that the offline CP inflation generalizes across controllers, we compute the CKRS for",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        135.07171630859375,
        522.0001220703125,
        144.82444763183594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "two references (Fig. 4, one orange, one blue) using the same offline-calibrated bounds; we visualize",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        148.6207275390625,
        522.0001831054688,
        158.3734588623047
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "additional CKRSs in Fig. 9. An NNV-only baseline (Nath et al., 2025) is much slower and more con-",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        162.17071533203125,
        522.000244140625,
        171.92344665527344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "servative, requiring 2153.45 s with an average log-volume of −30.32. Overall, these results show",
      "bbox": [
        90.0,
        174.66152954101562,
        522.000244140625,
        193.5888214111328
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "our method’s efficiency, tightness, and offline CP generalization for high-dimensional systems.",
